Here are the two files. I left out both operations requests, for these reasons:

- **Log file:** the component targets `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI, so it has no filesystem to write to.
- **Metadata fetch:** the node's contract grants only `state-rw`. An `http-client` import would give it authority it wasn't granted, and it would send input text to an external service.

If you want either one, it needs to be added to the node's declared capabilities in the graph first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in &published.considered {
                state_rw::put(id, "1");
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

